[ ] Make freshness worktree-relative =contextual-freshness $Introduce stable linked-worktree identity and represent reconciliation as a claim/evidence/finding assessment in a worktree context rather than one global mutable verdict. Preserve one shared claim corpus while preventing divergent worktrees from overwriting each other’s latest assessment. Keep historical logs replayable. Acceptance: the two-worktree characterization turns green; one shared claim can simultaneously project current and stale in different worktrees; bounded status/delta name their context; restart preserves both assessments; existing single-worktree semantics and tests remain intact.$ !1 +implementation ^2026-09-13T22:19 <coordination-contract #01a09e5a-f70e-7e22-996e-974957d84e4b
[ ] Add durable workstreams and resumable sessions =workstreams-sessions $Add durable workstreams as the owner of intended outcomes and ephemeral opaque sessions as resumable attribution contexts attached to a workstream and worktree. Attribute new meaningful records without fabricating provenance for historical events; project actor/harness labels and last_seen only as estimates. Acceptance: a replacement session resumes the same workstream after server restart; two sessions retain distinct worktree-local attention; shared knowledge remains discoverable; request/response MCP works without heartbeat or push; legacy event logs replay unchanged.$ !2 +implementation ^2026-09-13T22:19 <contextual-freshness #01a09e5b-0f34-7260-a79e-17f2d5b782be
[ ] Declare capabilities and advisory scopes atomically =coordination-declarations $Expose bounded MCP operations for a workstream to declare intended capability/outcome, external work item, integration target, and mutation or review paths. Declaration and its ranked overlap snapshot must be one serialized kernel operation; overlap remains advisory and distinguishes reader/reviewer/writer relationships. Acceptance: concurrent declarations cannot both receive a falsely clean snapshot; path and capability overlap are reported separately with omission counts; disjoint scopes remain possible; bypassed Git changes appear as unassociated repository divergence, not invented activity.$ !2 +implementation ^2026-09-13T22:19 <workstreams-sessions #01a09e5b-265f-7713-8099-6c3e65984d37
[ ] Add merge-aware dependencies and structured handoff =coordination-handoff $Let one workstream depend on another promised capability and plan around its integration target. Add restart-safe workstream states, dependency edges, checkpoint handoff, residual risks, and a receiving or unassigned responsibility target without creating a general mailbox. Git must verify branch/revision reachability before an integration is projected as landed. Acceptance: a dependent agent can wait, discover readiness, update its worktree, verify the landed revision, re-assess shared claims, and resume; handoff transfers responsibility but never freshness or truth.$ !2 +implementation ^2026-09-13T22:19 <coordination-declarations #01a09e5b-3aae-78c1-b96a-102173308713
[ ] Prove swarm coordination across harnesses and worktrees =coordination-dogfood $Run the charter walking skeleton with two different harnesses in linked Git worktrees on consequential repository work. Agent A produces a declared capability; Agent B discovers it, records a dependency instead of duplicating it, continues disjoint work, then resumes after Git-verified integration and local freshness reassessment. Measure false-current/false-stale results, overlap warnings, attribution gaps, bypasses, bookkeeping, latency, and context cost. Acceptance: the scenario succeeds with request/response MCP only and yields a field report plus a keep/change/reject architecture decision.$ !1 +evaluation ^2026-09-13T22:19 <coordination-handoff #01a09e5b-51d9-74d2-8c54-6cbe91a747ec
[x] Document the constructive collective agency perspective =collective-agency-perspective $User-requested design discussion, completed 2026-09-14 in knowledge/design/agent-perspective.md. Distinguishes METR findings, current documented workspace capabilities, accepted coordination requirements, and unapproved research proposals. Adds a cost-aware evaluation with wrong-but-current beliefs, handoff and scope-expansion probes. No implementation or roadmap change; contextual-freshness remains the highest-priority ready implementation action.$ +documentation ^2026-09-14T10:13 #01a0a0e8-b119-7fa0-83b7-b846d42b3123
[-] Reconcile the collective-agency proposal with independent review =collective-agency-review $Await the owner-arranged Claude review of knowledge/design/agent-perspective.md, then reconcile specific criticisms against evidence. Preserve accepted/rejected/unresolved recommendations and ask the owner to settle consequential scope choices; review is not automatic approval. Clarify the boundary: Clearhead owns commitments, priorities, action predecessors and lifecycle; Workspace owns execution workstreams, evidence, contextual assessments and operational dependencies. Workstream ready does not mean action complete; integration reachability does not prove acceptance; an external reference does not grant permissions. Examine objective revision/cancellation and cross-tool partial failure without promising automatic synchronization. Acceptance: a cited review response records dispositions and remaining questions; no unapproved architecture expansion.$ !2 +design ^2026-09-14T10:19 #01a0a0ee-330e-75c0-a181-a8add9b72f0a
[ ] Specify a falsifiable collective-agency evaluation =collective-agency-protocol $After review disposition, write a bounded evaluation protocol before running the experiment. Compare one capable agent, agents with ordinary messaging, and agents with messaging plus Workspace on matched foreign-repository maintenance tasks. Specify model mix, comparable total budgets, repeated trials/order controls, independent acceptance checks, baseline artifacts, and cost accounting including coordination and human intervention. Include worker replacement, producer/consumer capability discovery, changed dependencies, a plausible wrong-but-current claim, peer-requested scope expansion, and owner revision/cancellation of the external action. State which controls are enforced by runtime versus merely recorded by Workspace. Define keep/change/reject criteria and stop budgets in advance, without arbitrary precision unsupported by a pilot. Obtain owner approval for task scope and spend before execution; retain the protocol even if no experiment is approved.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-14T10:19 <collective-agency-review #01a0a0ee-331e-7393-8155-5026150db00c
[ ] Evaluate collective agency against simpler baselines =collective-agency-evaluation $Run only after the existing cross-harness coordination dogfood passes and the owner approves the evaluation protocol, external-effect scope and resource budget. Follow collective-agency-protocol, retain failed and inconclusive trials, and report verified outcome quality, wrong accepted claims, stale reliance, duplicate work, integration rework, human interventions, unauthorized effects, latency and total cost. Distinguish freshness detection from detecting false reasoning on unchanged evidence; distinguish declared readiness, Git landing and externally accepted completion. Produce a field report and a proposed keep/change/reject decision. Do not infer broad swarm superiority from one task or convert tentative recommendations into accepted architecture without owner decision.$ !2 +evaluation ^2026-09-14T10:19 <collective-agency-protocol <coordination-dogfood #01a0a0ee-3329-7433-b8a4-447f7e0d9369
